{
  "id": "cicd-codepipeline-ec2",
  "name": "CI/CD: CodeCommit → CodePipeline → CodeBuild → CodeDeploy",
  "category": "CI/CD & Developer Tools",
  "difficulty": "Intermediate",
  "description": "A push to CodeCommit starts CodePipeline. CodeBuild runs the buildspec, and CodeDeploy rolls the revision out one instance at a time to two EC2 web servers in private subnets behind an ALB. Each service has its own least-privilege service role.",
  "learningOutcome": "Select the repository and choose Push commit (or Run pipeline on the pipeline). Then break it: fail the build, uninstall the CodeDeploy agent on one instance, remove the NAT gateway route, or detach a service role, and see which stage stops and why.",
